.TH LUXEDM 1 "September 2026" "LuxeDM 1.4.1+luxe10"
.SH NAME
luxedm \- lightweight X11 display manager for Lumen and Luxe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxedm
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR theme ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR width x height ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LuxeDM authenticates users with PAM, starts X11 sessions listed in
/usr/share/xsessions, and presents the configured Luxe theme. Before the
greeter is drawn, the configured display setup command attaches eligible
secondary GPU output providers and enables connected RandR outputs. The
packaged helper arranges them temporarily from left to right; the authenticated
session may then restore its own display layout.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The
.B display_setup_cmd
setting in /etc/luxedm.conf names the command run after the X server is ready
and before monitor viewports are discovered. An empty value disables this
step. The command is split into arguments and executed directly without a
shell.
.SH FILES
/etc/luxedm.conf, /etc/pam.d/luxedm, /usr/share/luxedm/themes
